  "context": "A country is considered \"landlocked\" if it does not have a coastline on the open ocean. Inland bodies of water do not count as open ocean. A country is \"double-landlocked\" if it is landlocked and every country it shares a land border with is also landlocked. The following border relationships and coastal statuses are established for a specific geographic region:\n- Russia, China, and Iran each have coastlines on the open ocean.\n- Afghanistan is landlocked.\n- Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, and Uzbekistan are landlocked.\n- Kazakhstan shares land borders with Russia, China, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan, and Turkmenistan.\n- Kyrgyzstan shares land borders with Kazakhstan, Uzbekistan, Tajikistan, and China.\n- Tajikistan shares land borders with Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, China, and Afghanistan.\n- Turkmenistan shares land borders with Kazakhstan, Uzbekistan, Afghanistan, and Iran.\n- Uzbekistan shares land borders with Kazakhstan, Tajikistan, Kyrgyzstan, Afghanistan, and Turkmenistan.",
  "question": "Based on the provided definitions and border relationships, which of the listed countries is double-landlocked?",
  "correct_answer": "Uzbekistan",
  "distractors": [
    "Kazakhstan",
    "Kyrgyzstan",
    "Turkmenistan"
  ]
}
